    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;9.02</strong> Clinical and morphological (imaging and pathomolecular) characteristics of hepatocellular adenoma (HCA)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Valerie Paradis",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 694.6pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"926\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 98.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"131\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Characteristics</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 596.45pt; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"795\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">HCA subtype</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; border: none; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">H-HCA</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IHCA</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">b-HCA and b-IHCA<sup>a</sup></span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">shHCA</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 98.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"131\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong>Relative frequency</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">30&ndash;35%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">35&ndash;40%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">b-HCA: 10%</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">b-IHCA: 10&ndash;15%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">5&ndash;10%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 98.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"131\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Molecular findings</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Biallelic inactivating mutations of <em>HNF1A</em>:</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Somatic mutations: 90% (mainly in women)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Germline mutations: 10% (MODY3)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">CYP1B1</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> mutations may predispose to H-HCA</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IL-6/JAK/STAT activation due to mutations:</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">IL6ST</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> coding gp130 (60%)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">FRK</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> (10%)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">STAT3</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> (5%)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">GNAS</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> (5%)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">JAK1</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> (3%)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">or chromosomal alterations</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">CTNNB1</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> activating mutations/deletions leading to different levels of &beta;-catenin pathway activation:</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Exon&nbsp;3 (other than Ser45): high level</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Exon&nbsp;3 Ser45: moderate to weak level</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Exon&nbsp;7/8: weak level</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Sonic hedgehog activation due to focal deletions fusing <em>INHBE</em> and <em>GLI1</em>; activation of the target gene <em>GLI1</em></span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 98.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"131\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong>MRI characteristics</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Typical (massive fat component):</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Diffuse and homogeneous signal dropout on T1-weighted images</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Usually moderate arterial enhancement, not persistent during the delayed phase</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Atypical if steatosis is absent</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Typical:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Hyperintense on T2, diffuse or predominant at the periphery (atoll sign)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Usually strong arterial enhancement, persistent in the delayed phase</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Hyperintensity on hepatobiliary phase signal in b-HCA with higher malignant risk</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Frequent fluid-filled cavities</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 98.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"131\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Clinical context</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Female patients, childbearing age</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Male patients (rare)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">MODY3 (both sexes; familial form)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Solitary, multiple, adenomatosis</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Female patients, childbearing age</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Male patients (rare)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Obesity, metabolic syndrome, alcohol</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Steatosis in background liver</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Solitary, multiple, adenomatosis</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Female patients, younger in exon&nbsp;3 Ser45 and exon&nbsp;7/8 mutated cases</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Male patients (more common compared with other subtypes)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Male hormones; metabolic diseases</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Solitary, rarely multiple</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Female patients, mostly aged &gt;&nbsp;40&nbsp;years; obesity; metabolic syndrome</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Solitary, multiple</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 98.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"131\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong>Histological features</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Typical: lobulated contours, diffuse steatosis (macro, microvacuolar), ballooned cells, clear cells, a few pseudoglands</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Microadenomas in background liver, particularly in adenomatosis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Non-typical: no (or minor) steatosis; myxoid stroma, heavy lipofuscin pigmentation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Typical: sinusoidal dilatation, congestion, foci of lymphocytic inflammation, thick arteries, ductular reaction, pseudoportal tracts</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Occasional: steatosis, fibrotic bands, nodular architecture (remodelling)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Non-typical: lack of one or several features</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Exon&nbsp;3 non-Ser45 mutation: often cytoarchitectural atypia, pseudoglands, pigments (lipofuscins, bile), focally decreased reticulin network<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">In exon&nbsp;3 Ser45 and exon&nbsp;7/8: frequent abnormal vessels in the HCA, usually near the rim</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Bland appearance; clear cells alternating with retracted, atrophic cells; vacuoles filled with blood or fibrin, large necrotic or haemorrhagic areas</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Steatosis and/or steatohepatitis in NT liver</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 98.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"131\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Immunomarkers (useful in practice)</span></strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Liver fatty acid&ndash;binding protein: absent in tumour (cytoplasmic and/or nuclear staining in normal liver)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">GS: absent or positive around veins, or scattered patchy staining</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">C-reactive protein and serum amyloid&nbsp;A positivity: usually diffuse, with sharp demarcation from adjacent liver (adjacent liver can be focally or diffusely positive in some cases with haemorrhage, general inflammation, previous embolization, etc.)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">GS: absent or positive around veins, mainly at the periphery of nodule, or scattered patchy staining</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">GS overexpression<sup>c</sup>, depending on the mutation types:</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Exon&nbsp;3 (other than Ser45): typically diffuse homogeneous staining (and often some nuclear &beta;-catenin positivity)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Exon&nbsp;3 Ser45: diffuse heterogeneous staining, starry-sky pattern (little or no nuclear &beta;-catenin)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Exon&nbsp;7/8: faint, with or without perivascular staining (no nuclear &beta;-catenin)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">In exon&nbsp;3 Ser45 and exon&nbsp;7/8: often GS+ rim and diffuse CD34+ in the HCA, except in the rim</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">ASS1 overexpression in T liver (not specific), compared with NT liver (in NT liver, ASS1 is expressed predominantly in periportal zones: honeycomb pattern)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">PTGDS overexpression in T (more specific but not sensitive enough)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">L-FABP often decreased (compared with NT liver)</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">All other HCA markers are unremarkable</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 98.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"131\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\"><strong>Risk of complications</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">All subtypes: haemorrhagic risk if &gt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;mm</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Low risk of HCC</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Low risk of HCC</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Exon&nbsp;3 non-Ser45 mutation: higher risk of HCC; lower in exon&nbsp;3 Ser45</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Exon&nbsp;7/8 mutation: no/low risk of HCC</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">Exon&nbsp;3 Ser45 and exon&nbsp;7/8: higher risk of clinically significant haemorrhage</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 149.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"199\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Hlk210053124;\">High risk of haemorrhage, even if &lt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;mm</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">b-HCA, &beta;-catenin-activated hepatocellular adenoma; b-IHCA, &beta;-catenin-activated inflammatory hepatocellular adenoma; GS, glutamine synthetase; HCC, hepatocellular carcinoma; IHCA, inflammatory hepatocellular adenoma; MODY3, maturity-onset diabetes of the young, type&nbsp;3; NT,&nbsp;non-tumoural; shHCA, sonic hedgehog hepatocellular adenoma; T,&nbsp;tumoural.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Associated features of b-HCA and IHCA. <sup>b</sup>Also referred to as borderline lesion or atypical hepatocellular neoplasm (not sufficient for the diagnosis of HCC). <sup>c</sup>In NT liver, GS is restricted to a few rows of perivenular hepatocytes; the pattern of GS staining often correlates well with mutation type, but exceptions can occur.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
